# ── Mission profile ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

msgid "section.mission_profile.title"
msgstr "Mission Profile"

msgid "section.mission_profile.intro"
msgstr ""
"The mission profile defines the sequence of flight phases from takeoff "
"to landing. Each segment contributes to the total weight fraction and "
"energy budget of the aircraft."

msgid "section.mission_profile.figure_caption"
msgstr "Mission altitude profile — altitude vs. cumulative range/time"

msgid "section.mission_profile.no_diagram_note"
msgstr "Mission profile diagram not available — run sizing first."

msgid "section.mission_profile.methodology"
msgstr ""
"The sizing methodology follows Sadraey 2020, Sec. 2.6-2.7, where each "
"segment contributes a weight fraction $${W_i/W_{i-1}}$$ to the overall "
"MTOW buildup. Fixed segments use tabulated fractions (Table 2.4); cruise "
"and loiter segments use the Breguet range/endurance equations."

# ── Weight breakdown ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.title"
msgstr "Weight Estimation"

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.no_result_note"
msgstr "Weight estimation results not available — run sizing first."

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.intro"
msgstr ""
"Takeoff weight is estimated using the iterative Breguet mission-fraction "
"method (Sadraey 2020, Sec. 2.6-2.7). The weight loop converges when "
"successive MTOW estimates differ by less than 0.1 g."

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.heading.mass_summary"
msgstr "Mass Summary"

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.heading.segment_fractions"
msgstr "Segment Weight Fractions"

msgid "section.weight_breakdown.segments_intro"
msgstr ""
"Each segment reduces the aircraft weight by its fraction "
"$${W_i/W_{i-1}}$$. The product of all fractions gives the overall "
"mission weight fraction (Sadraey 2020, Sec. 2.6, Table 2.4)."

